{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-index-range","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0300","math_ordinal":183,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The family consists of X_1 through X_n and the displayed linear combination has coefficients alpha_1 through alpha_n; alpha_0 is extraneous while alpha_1 is required.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt271.tex:271","source_normalized_sha256":"1a41c5b04fec69f14523727801b84556b51d2d369cb45697769de2e32a6ba6e3","source_text":"for all $\\alpha_0,\\ldots,\\alpha_n\\in\\Bbb R$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt271.tex:269","target_normalized_sha256":"1d3accc8b3637dd146cbab1155971e56576b645349d5a8ea34ae1a67b8b0a263","target_text":"untuk semua $\\alpha_1,\\ldots,\\alpha_n\\in\\Bbb R$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S271"}
{"classification":"mathematical-undefined-measure-symbol","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0301","math_ordinal":328,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The surrounding result declares Lebesgue measure mu_L and the next displayed identity integrates f against mu_L; no measure named bare mu is bound in this argument.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt271.tex:491-492","source_normalized_sha256":"492247e1bab15272d1e53b8015c042bf6fa0cb8f23ec52cad93d6ba80dafb804","source_text":"the indefinite-integral measure over $\\mu$ associated with $f$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt271.tex:492-493","target_normalized_sha256":"247bec05dfd02479e4fd8a8f5e4229ccd52f456f8a7ce2b8014ba26b684ecb82","target_text":"ukuran integral tak tentu di atas $\\mu_L$ yang berkaitan dengan $f$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S271"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-local-function-symbol","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0302","math_ordinal":374,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The parenthetical argument is proving integrability of the fixed summand g_k, whose definition makes it zero outside phi[D_k]; the total density g generally has support on the other phi[D_j].","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt271.tex:545-546","source_normalized_sha256":"cd0aa9856147b6c5b4ff2b7dfee5da20aa38253099ef1b4a64aced233c9afe29","source_text":"$g$ is zero off $\\phi[D_k]$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt271.tex:545-547","target_normalized_sha256":"c1c366f26da4333411ab8b08195752361b317cc2454a5159672ac2ac4d043588","target_text":"$g_k$ nol di luar $\\phi[D_k]$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S271"}
{"classification":"mathematical-swapped-coordinate-arguments","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0303","math_ordinal":566,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The mixed lower-left corner of the rectangle is (beta_1,alpha_2), not (alpha_2,beta_1); the latter reverses the two coordinate roles.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt271.tex:760-761","source_normalized_sha256":"02702ad1fe0789ca7945f479bb79ebf49c577730134c9d871c22239c9ece5d63","source_text":"$F(\\alpha_1,\\alpha_2)+F(\\beta_1,\\beta_2)\\ge F(\\alpha_1,\\beta_2)+F(\\alpha_2,\\beta_1)$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt271.tex:757-758","target_normalized_sha256":"1c20b154df49bca441ad4c8ada4ecf145f5c49194c76ce9394b08213a25ccc7a","target_text":"$F(\\alpha_1,\\alpha_2)+F(\\beta_1,\\beta_2)\\ge F(\\alpha_1,\\beta_2)+F(\\beta_1,\\alpha_2)$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S271"}
{"classification":"mathematical-swapped-coordinate-arguments","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0304","math_ordinal":579,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH27-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The hint must use the same four rectangle corners as the corrected condition; its second mixed corner is (beta_1,alpha_2).","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt271.tex:770-771","source_normalized_sha256":"f27f1e124385659ab65b2f06f6da7cd88a94441b78f8554d264c516403673b65","source_text":"$\\lambda\\ocint{a,b}=F(\\alpha_1,\\alpha_2)+F(\\beta_1,\\beta_2)-F(\\alpha_1,\\beta_2)-F(\\alpha_2,\\beta_1)$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt271.tex:767-768","target_normalized_sha256":"05cb6065f34a4d089476fe94feaca64f016d996150d2c09446f7687bbe4ea897","target_text":"$\\lambda\\ocint{a,b}=F(\\alpha_1,\\alpha_2)+F(\\beta_1,\\beta_2)-F(\\alpha_1,\\beta_2)-F(\\beta_1,\\alpha_2)$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S271"}
